cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use asmsense, its dataset or its baselines, please cite it as below."
title: "asmsense: naming and describing functions in stripped x86-64 binaries"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: krxi
repository-code: "https://github.com/krxi/asmsense"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/krxi123/asmsense"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A dataset, evaluation protocol and baselines for recovering function names and
  one-sentence descriptions from stripped x86-64 binaries. The v4 data covers
  228,177 functions from 341 permissively licensed C projects at five optimization
  levels, with a project-level split whose test projects are little-known and
  recent to limit memorization. Baselines include large open models with and
  without call context or decompiled code, and Qwen3-8B LoRA adapters.
keywords:
  - reverse engineering
  - binary analysis
  - function name recovery
  - stripped binaries
  - decompilation
  - dataset
  - large language models
references:
  - type: data
    title: "asmsense dataset"
    authors:
